prettier

basic structure of html
declaration ---> it tell the type and version(5) of doc to the browser
<!DOCTYPE html>

1.ctrl / ---> comments
2.if we want paragraph type "Lorem"
3. basic tags
   <html> </html> ---> root element
   <head> </head> ---> meta data
   <title> </title> ---> title of the page
   <body> </body> ---> content of the page
4. heading tags
   h1 - h6
   <h1> - largest heading </h1>
   <h2> - second largest heading </h2>
   <h3> - third largest heading </h3> 
   <h4> - fourth largest heading </h4>
   <h5> - fifth largest heading </h5>
   <h6> - smallest heading </h6>
5. paragraph tag
   <p> </p> ---> paragraph
6. comments
   <!--  -->
7. line break
   <br> ---> line break
8. horizontal rule
   <hr> ---> horizontal line
9. closing tags
   </br> ---> closing line break
   </hr> ---> closing horizontal rule
10. indentation
    - it is used to make the code more readable and organized
    - it is not mandatory but it is a good practice
11. self closing tags
    - some tags do not have closing tags
    - they are called self closing tags
    - example: <br>, <hr>, <img>, <input>
12. semantic tags
    - semantic tags are used to give meaning to the content
    - example: <header>, <footer>, <article>, <section>, <nav>
13.anchor tag
    - <a> </a> ---> anchor tag
    - it is used to create links
    - example: <a href="https://www.google.com">Google</a>
14. absolute url
    - it is used to link to external websites
    - example: <a href="https://www.google.com">Google</a>
15. relative url
    - it is used to link to internal pages 
16. attributes
    - attributes are used to provide additional information about an element
    - example: <a href="https://www.google.com" target="_blank">Google</a>
    - common attributes: id, class, src, alt, href, target
17.href attribute
    - it is used to specify the URL of the page the link goes to
    - example: <a href="https://www.google.com">Google</a>
18.target attribute
    - it is used to specify where to open the linked document
    - example: <a href="https://www.google.com" target="_blank">Google</a>
19.list tags
    - <ul> </ul> ---> unordered list
    - <ol> </ol> ---> ordered list
    - <li> </li> ---> list item
